  "question": {
    "text": "Two spherical stars <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> emit blackbody radiation. The radius of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> is 400 times that of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> emits <math><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></math> times the power emitted from <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> . The ratio <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#955;</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#955;</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math> of their wavelengths <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#955;</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mrow></msub></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#955;</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mrow></msub></math> at which the peaks occur in their respective radiation curves is",
    "image": null
